#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:2
msgid "Creating a Release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:5
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:7
msgid "Push access to the ``syncthing`` repo, for pushing a new tag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:9
msgid "SSH account on the signing server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:12
msgid "Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:14
msgid ""
"Make sure the build seems sane. I.e. the build is clean on the build server, "
"the integration tests pass without complaints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:17
msgid "Update the documentation and translations, and commit the result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:19
msgid ""
"$ ./build.sh prerelease\n"
"$ git commit -m \"Translation and docs update\"\n"
"$ git push"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:25
msgid ""
"Create a new, signed tag on master, with the version as comment, and push it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:28
msgid ""
"$ git tag -a -s -m v0.10.15 v0.10.15\n"
"$ git push --tags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:33
msgid ""
"(The tag is signed with your personal key. The binary releases will be "
"signed by the Syncthing Release key later. I use `git autotag <https://"
"github.com/calmh/git-autotag>`__ to do this correcly with minimal pain.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:38
msgid ""
"Trigger the ``syncthing-release`` job for the newly created tag and wait for "
"it to complete successfully before moving on. This builds the ``syncthing-"
"release-windows``, ``syncthing-release-mac`` and ``syncthing-release-"
"debian`` jobs as well, and these must succeed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:43
msgid ""
"Run ``go run script/changelog.go`` (in the repo) to create the changelog "
"comparison from the previous release. Copy to clipboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:46
msgid ""
"On the Github releases page, select the newly pushed tag and hit \"Edit "
"Tag\". Set the \"Release title\" to the same version as the tag, paste in "
"the changelog from above, and publish the release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:50
msgid ""
"On the signing server, logged in via ssh, run ``sign-upload-release``. This "
"will download the build artefacts from Jenkins, sign all the binaries, "
"create the sha1sum and sha256sum files, sign them with the release GPG key "
"and upload the whole shebang to Github."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:55
msgid "Verify it looks sane on the releases page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/release-creation.rst:57
msgid ""
"Then run ``sign-upload-debian`` which does the same for the Debian packages "
"-- downloads them, signs the package archive, and pushes the new archive to "
"the web server."
msgstr ""
